rs because they wanted horrible  things like could we say that displaying  Nazi flags just because they lost is  just its history like there was a German  military and it's just wrecking like  okay guys it's an extreme example but I  find it to be in very very poor taste  now this gets us to NASCAR NASCAR in the  United States is not known for being  made up of the most progressive people  now I'm not saying NASCAR fans are all  racists but it's certainly a sport that  leans more conservative in terms of its  fan base and it's one of the few places  where Donald Trump can actually get  himself a crowd that cheers instead of a  crowd that boos and it is a place where  unfortunately Confederate flags are  certainly more common than in other  sports you don't tend to see Confederate  flags at NBA games you don't tend to see  Confederate flags at major league soccer  matches and as far as I know they  wouldn't even be allowed in to be  perfectly frank but you do see them at  NASCAR races until now NASCAR has now  banned the display of the Confederate  flag at all events and properties and  notably NASCAR also removed its rule  that says racing team members have to  stand for the national anthem and we've  seen a number of sports leagues now say  you know if you don't want to stand you  actually don't have to stand so every  indication here is NASCAR sees what's  happening nationally since the killing  of George Floyd Bubba Wallace one of  their racers has been very supportive a  drivers I think they're called has-been  shows what I know has been very  supportive of the protests and they are  making a decision that there is going to  be no more Confederate stuff at their  races now is it because everybody  involved  morally believes that there shouldn't be  Confederate flags I don't know certainly  they've made the business decision that  there will be no more confederate flags  they're not everybody's happy NASCAR  Truck Series driver ray Sorelli  Ciccarelli wrote on his Facebook page  he's gonna quit after this season  because Confederate flags have been  banned have fun buddy don't let the door  hit you on the way out and then here's  the real amazing contrast look at the  last 24 hours in NASCAR  okay and compare that to the last 24  hours of Trump Trump putting out a  statement and tweeting that he will not  change the names of Confederacy themed  military bases saying quote it has been  suggested that we should rename as many  as 10 of our legendary military bases  such as Fort Bragg in North Carolina  Fort Hood in Texas Fort Benning in  Georgia these monumental and very  powerful bases have become part of a  great American heritage and a history of  winning victory and freedom the United  States of America trained and deployed  these our heroes on these hallowed  grounds and won two world wars therefore  my administration will not even consider  the renaming of these magnificent and  fabled military installations our  history as the greatest nation in the  world will not be tampered with respect  our military now what's funny about  respect our military is that remember  the Union won the Civil War meaning that  the military should be respected the  military that should be respected is the  military that fought against the  Confederacy because we won the Union won  so when you name the fort's after the  side that lost that was killing the  precursor to our current military the  Confederacy that fought for slavery  doesn't really make a lot of sense  because you've named forts after people  who were against our military they did  not respect our military so listen this  is not the biggest issue I don't really  care what the fort's are called although  it doesn't make a lot of sense to me  that we named him after the losers who  wanted to keep slaves but who would have  guessed as Barack Obama was leaving  office that during the subsequent  presidential term NASCAR would take the  more progressive stance of banning the  Confederate flag compared to the  president who defends Confederacy era  statues figures heroes whatever they  like to call him Republican group the  Lincoln project which is a Republican  group that opposes Trump has now come  out and said Trump is the Confederacy's  second prize  this is a Republican group which put out  a statement where they said we never  imagined when we named our initiative to  defeat the re-election of Trump the  Lincoln project that the president would  go as far as honoring the Confederate  generals who fought against the United  States to preserve slavery and uphold  white supremacy for all intents and  purposes Trump today became the  Confederacy's second president we cannot  allow this and then they go on to say we  need help from Republicans to remove  Donald Trump in November strange times  but I believe the decision by NASCAR is  the correct one whatever their reasons  for doing it and it's probably a mix of  understanding the way society is going  combined with the fact that it's  probably a bad PR move to continue  having these flags displayed they did  ultimately come to the right decision
 

